   'High-intensity statin. Minimal CYP2C9 metabolism (10%). Not a prodrug. Oral bioavailability ~20%. Half-life ~19h allows once-daily dosing. Lower CYP-mediated interaction potential compared to simvastatin.',
   'Cefaleia\nMialgia\nDor abdominal\nNáuseas\nAumento das transaminases\nRaramente: miopatia/rabdomiólise',
